# Build context for the CodeProof image (see Dockerfile and DOCKER.md).
#
# The image bakes the committed project and its evidence. Local working data that .gitignore keeps
# out of the repository is kept out of the image too: run output, probe checkouts (local copies of
# analyzed repositories) and the benchmark's installed dependencies are not project source.
#
# .git stays in the context on purpose: `make integrity`, `make replay` and `make score` verify
# the committed evidence against real git revisions, and the image is meant to run those gates.

# Per-machine linked-worktree metadata (agent worktrees on the build host), not project content.
.git/worktrees

# Installed dependencies and build output (the project itself has zero runtime dependencies).
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets are passed at runtime, never baked. Only the documented example stays in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# reports/: same committed whitelist as .gitignore; every other run directory stays out.
reports/*
!reports/README.md
!reports/golden
!reports/golden/**
!reports/real-world
!reports/real-world/**
!reports/controlled-verifier
!reports/controlled-verifier/**
!reports/historical
!reports/historical/**
!reports/probes
!reports/probes/**
!reports/ablations
!reports/ablations/**
!reports/model-ablation
!reports/model-ablation/**
!reports/self-analysis
!reports/self-analysis/**
!reports/three-way
!reports/three-way/**
!reports/chunked-scan
!reports/chunked-scan/**
!reports/v0.2.0
!reports/v0.2.0/**
!reports/final
!reports/final/**
# Probe checkouts: local copies of the analyzed upstream repositories, not project evidence.
reports/**/_repo

# Local report note that .gitignore drops by name (working file, not committed evidence).
reports/probes/agy-batch3.md
